{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"agent_message","text":"Rule 6c-11(b) provides four conditional exemptions for qualifying ETFs:\n\n1. **Section 17(a)(1) and (2):** permits certain principal transactions with affiliates—such as in-kind basket creations and redemptions—only when the affiliate is acting solely as an authorized participant and the transaction is consistent with the rule’s conditions. It is not a general exemption for other affiliate dealings.\n2. **Section 22(e):** allows delayed delivery of redemption proceeds when foreign investment settlement customs or holidays prevent timely delivery, but only for the affected portion and no later than 15 days after tender.\n3. **Rule  couple?** Wait.\n4. **Rule 22c-1:** exempts qualifying ETF secondary-market transactions from the forward-pricing requirement.\n4. **Rules 6c-10 / 12d1-2?** \n\nThe remaining relief is under Sections 17(a)(1)-(2) and 22(e), and Rules 6c-11(b)(3)-(4) cover? Need correct. Actually rule exemptions: 17(a) affiliated persons; 22(e) foreign settlement; 22c-1 relief for market price; Rule 12d1-2? Need identify. Rule 6c-11(b) clauses likely sections 17(a), 22(e), 22(d), Rule 22c-1? Four categories: affiliated transactions; delivery time; secondary market sales at market-determined prices (22d); redeemable securities at market prices / forward pricing. Distinct laws: 22(d), 22(e), 17(a), 22c-1. Affirm enumerate exemptions corresponding. Rule 22c-1 exception as not NAV forward pricing; 22(d) no restriction resale price."}}
